db-cmd-inquiry-objects-prompt = Select objects:
db-cmd-not-closed = Object {$id} is not closed, so it has no area.
db-cmd-points-too-few = An area needs at least three points, or a closed object.
db-cmd-no-curve = The object has no curve geometry to measure.
db-setting-draft-layer-current = The current layer, which new entities take.
db-setting-draft-color-current = The current color: 0 for by block, 256 for by layer, or a palette index.
db-setting-draft-linetype-current = The current linetype: ByLayer, ByBlock or the name of a linetype.
db-setting-draft-lineweight-current = The current lineweight: -1 by layer, -2 by block, -3 the default, or hundredths of a millimeter.
db-setting-draft-transparency-current = The current transparency in percent: -1 by layer, -2 by block.
db-setting-draft-linetype-global-scale = The global scale of linetype patterns.
db-setting-draft-linetype-object-scale = The scale of linetype patterns for new objects.
db-setting-draft-units-length = The length format: 1 scientific, 2 decimal, 3 engineering, 4 architectural, 5 fractional.
db-setting-draft-units-length-precision = The number of decimal places in lengths.
db-setting-draft-units-angle = The angle format code; decimal degrees is 0.
db-setting-draft-units-angle-precision = The number of decimal places in angles.
db-setting-draft-units-insertion = The insertion unit of the drawing's model space, read only.
db-setting-draft-angle-base = The angle of zero, in radians.
db-setting-draft-angle-direction = The angle direction: 0 counterclockwise, 1 clockwise.
db-setting-draft-limits-check = Whether point entry outside the drawing limits is refused.
db-setting-draft-limits-min = The lower-left corner of the drawing limits.
db-setting-draft-limits-max = The upper-right corner of the drawing limits.
db-setting-draft-point-style = The display style of point entities.
db-setting-draft-point-size = The display size of point entities.
db-setting-snap-object-running = The running object snap set, as a sum of the snap bits.
db-setting-draft-ortho = Whether ortho constrains the pick to the axes of the coordinate system.
db-setting-draft-polar-on = Whether polar tracking is on.
db-setting-draft-polar-increment = The polar angle increment, in degrees.
db-setting-draft-polar-additional = Additional polar angles, in degrees, separated by commas.
db-setting-draft-snap-on = Whether the snap grid constrains the pick.
db-setting-draft-snap-spacing = The snap spacing along the X and Y axes.
db-setting-draft-snap-base = The origin of the snap grid.
db-setting-draft-snap-angle = The rotation of the snap grid, in radians.
db-setting-draft-grid-on = Whether the grid is displayed.
db-setting-draft-grid-spacing = The spacing of the displayed grid along the X and Y axes.
db-setting-command-echo = Whether prompts and input of script commands are echoed to the history.
db-setting-snap-object-on = Whether the running object snap set applies; toggled as a whole without losing the modes.
db-setting-snap-override-typed-first = Whether a typed coordinate takes precedence over a running snap at the same place.
db-setting-snap-aperture = The pick aperture in pixels.
db-cmd-script-pending = The script ends while command {$command} waits at prompt {$prompt} for an answer; the command did not run.
db-cmd-script-directive = UNDO and REDO take no count or a positive whole number of steps.
db-cmd-pick-none = No object lies at the point given for a pick.
db-cmd-setting-not-transparent = The setting {$name} cannot be set while another command waits at a prompt.
db-cmd-script-limit = The script exceeds the limit {$limit} (at most {$max}).
db-setting-snap-object-geometric-center = Object snap to the geometric center (kept outside the running-set header bits).
db-cmd-ucs-handedness = The third point of a coordinate system must be counterclockwise from the X direction.
